-- title:
--   Smooth-point stalks from the affine chart at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and an auxiliary prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ is fixed. Further data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime` (the image of $q$ is a non-unit of $A$); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. of the places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and have $w$-value of the geometric $j$-generator in the supersingular $j$-set; a chosen element $s \in W$; the inclusion `hle` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-fields $F_j :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the field generated by the $q$-expansions of $j(dz)$, $d \mid M'$) into $F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$); a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $F_j$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $F_j$ with a surjective residue map onto the reduced field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with orders of places); and the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $F_j$, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   The base-layer data consist of: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; the approximation hypothesis `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$; a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ whose image is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cutting out $A$ (`hAb`), and a nonzero generator $\varpi_b$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The field $F$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$. The assertion is then: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, the package of hypotheses below implies the package of conclusions below.
--
--   The hypothesis package has nine conjuncts. (K1) The compositum of $F_0$ with the constants, $k_0(\operatorname{range}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F)) \sqcup F_0$, is all of $F$. (K2) For $x \in k_0$: the image of $x$ lies in $A$ if and only if its image in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$. (K3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring. (K4) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (K5) There is $t \in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients have image in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, then every coefficient of $p$ has image in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal. (LD) For every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $F_j$ lies in `R₀.integers`, if $g$ has non-negative order at every place of $F_j$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $j$ has non-negative order, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ in $F$ lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with image in $A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference (image of $g$) $-\, c$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal. (EQ) For every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $F_0$ into itself and, on $F_0$, preserves membership in $W_0$ in both directions. (LI) For every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every family $a$ of elements of $k_0(\text{image of } K') \sqcup F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, all $a_i$ vanish. (CHART) There are a subring $B$ of $F$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that: the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a$ under $K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$; $B$ is contained in $k_0(\text{image of } K_b) \sqcup F_0$ and every element of that compositum is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\varpi_b$, in the sense that $f \in W_0$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $\varpi_b \nmid h$; the image of $j$ in $F$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and finally, for every algebra structure of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2` on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the $C_s$-fixed subfield of the Drinfeld function field) such that $\#C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, $\ker \rho = (\varpi_b)$, $\rho$ restricted to $A_b$ is reduction $A_b \to \kappa$ followed by the structure map, every element of the target is a quotient of elements of the image of $\rho$, the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements of the fixed field whose underlying element of the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of the coordinate ring, and $\rho$ intertwines $f \mapsto$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f$ with the action [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) of $(\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma), 1) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. Here `placeWidthChar q M' s` is `jWidthChar q` of the value of the geometric $j$-generator at $s$, divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; for $q = 2$ the numerator is $12$ if that value is $0$ and $1$ otherwise.
--
--   The conclusion package repeats the seven conjuncts (K1), (K2), (K3), (K4), (K5), (LD), (EQ), (LI) verbatim, and replaces (CHART) by the following clause about prolongations. For every type $F_{SS}$ which is a field and an algebra over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $F_{SS}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ with a surjective residue map to $F_{SS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$), such that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in$ `R.integers` if and only if $f \in W_0$, two things hold.
--
--   First, the identification of the residue field: for every algebra structure of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e : F_{SS} \cong$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with $\#C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, assuming that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers` and that $(\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma), 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the automorphism of $F_{SS}$ induced by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` on residues corresponds under $e$ to the action [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) of $(\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma), 1)$ on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Second, there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$, an assignment $Q \mapsto S_Q$ of subrings of $F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q : A_b[X] \to S_Q$ and $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \kappa$ for each $Q$, and an assignment $Q \mapsto D_Q$ of sets of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the following properties. The cardinality of $N$ is $q + 1$. There is a subring $B$ of $F$ contained in `R.integers`, contained in $S_Q$ for every $Q \notin N$, and such that every $z \in F_{SS}$ lying in the valuation subring of every place $Q \notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$. For every $Q \notin N$: the image in $F$ of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C a)$ is that image; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; $S_Q$ is local with $\ker \chi_Q$ its maximal ideal; $S_Q$ is contained in $k_0(\text{image of } K_b) \sqcup F_0$ and every element of that compositum is a quotient of two elements of $S_Q$ with nonzero denominator; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; every element of $S_Q$ lies in `R.integers`, and such an element lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` exactly when it is divisible by $\varphi_Q(C \varpi_b)$; for every $f \in S_Q$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in the residue field of $Q$ is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q$'s residue field; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; and $D_Q$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which are rational, for which every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P$-value in $A$, and for which, for every $f \in S_Q$, the $A$-valuation of the $P$-value of $f$ is $< 1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f) = 0$. Moreover the discs are pairwise disjoint: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, if some place $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ then $Q = Q'$. The discs avoid the cusps: for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, the $P$-order of the image of $j$ in $F$ is non-negative. Finally, the whole configuration is equivariant: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $\tau$ preserving `R.integers`, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ` permutes $N$ (for every place $Q$, its translate lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does), and for $Q \notin N$ one has `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (Db Q) = Db (R.resAut τ • Q)`, where `smulDisc τ D = {P | τ⁻¹ • P ∈ D}`.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case, at the rigid auxiliary level given by $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ with $\ell_g \mid M'$, of the passage from an affine chart of the supersingular component of the descended semistable model of $X(q^2M')$ to the base-layer data attached to that component: the identification of its residue field with a $C_s$-fixed subfield of the Drinfeld function field, equivariantly for the level automorphisms, together with étale coordinates, residue characters and residue discs at the reduced places off the $q+1$ ends. It feeds the assembling statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart).
